Work with a Top 20 CPA and advisory firm that Accounts for Anything. &nbsp;Aprio has 40 U.S. office locations, as well as international office locations and more than 3,200 team members that speak 60+ languages across the globe. &nbsp;By bringing together proven expertise, deep understanding, and strategic foresight for fast-growing industries, Aprio ensures clients are prepared for wherever life or business may take them. Discover a top-rated culture, vast growth opportunities and your next big career move with Aprio. Job Summary&nbsp; Aprio is seeking a Private Client Tax Manager, to lead a dedicated team of tax professionals delivering compliance, consulting, and planning services for individuals, trusts, and closely held businesses. In this role, you will develop and implement forward-thinking tax strategies, manage complex client relationships, and serve as a trusted advisor in a dynamic regulatory environment. You will drive business development, mentor and develop team members, and play a meaningful role in the continued growth of Aprio's private client practice. &nbsp; &nbsp; 
 What You'll Gain/ Impact Opportunity to lead and shape a high-performing team of tax professionals in a growing, high-impact practice Exposure to sophisticated, multi-faceted engagements spanning individuals, trusts, and closely held businesses Ability to directly influence client outcomes through strategic tax planning and advisory services A platform for business development and expanded client relationship ownership within a Top 20 CPA firm Key Responsibilities Review complex individual tax returns (Form 1040), trust returns (Form 1041), and business returns (Forms 1065, 1120S), ensuring accuracy and compliance with federal and state tax laws Lead tax planning engagements for individuals and small business owners, advising on strategies including asset protection, succession planning, and retirement optimization Manage multiple client relationships and engagements simultaneously, monitoring deadlines, budgets, and deliverables to ensure timely, high-quality service Supervise and mentor staff preparing returns, providing technical guidance, quality review, and meaningful developmental feedback Collaborate with internal teams and external advisors to deliver integrated, holistic client solutions Identify and pursue business development opportunities, including expanding services with existing clients and participating in networking and prospecting activities Contribute to internal training and professional development initiatives to strengthen team capability Candidate Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field Minimum 5 years of experience in individual tax, trusts, and small business returns in public accounting Strong communication skills with demonstrated ability to build and maintain trust with clients Preferred: CPA license or EA designation Preferred: Master's degree in Taxation or related field Leadership Skills Proven ability to lead, coach, and develop a team of tax professionals across multiple concurrent engagements Effective delegation and workload management skills with a focus on team accountability and quality Demonstrated ability to mentor junior staff and provide meaningful, growth-oriented feedback Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to navigate difficult client and team conversations with professionalism and sound judgment Technical Skills Proficiency in tax compliance and review software (e.g., CCH Axcess, GoSystem Tax RS, or equivalent platforms) Strong working knowledge of federal and state individual, trust, and pass-through entity tax compliance Familiarity with financial planning concepts, including asset protection, succession planning, and retirement optimization strategies Ability to leverage technology and digital tools to enhance client service delivery and engagement efficiency 
 $98,500 - $164,000 a year The salary range for this opportunity is stated above. As such, an actual salary may fall closer to one or the other end of the range, and in certain circumstances, may wind up being outside of the listed salary range.&nbsp; 
 Why work for Aprio: Whether you are just starting out, looking to advance into management or searching for your next leadership role, Aprio offers an opportunity to grow with a future-focused, innovative firm. &nbsp; &nbsp; Perks/Benefits we offer for full-time team members: - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance on the first day of employment - Flexible Spending Account and Dependent Care Account - 401k with Profit Sharing - 9+ holidays and discretionary time off structure - Parental Leave â coverage for both primary and secondary caregivers - Tuition Assistance Program and CPA support program with cash incentive upon completion - Discretionary incentive compensation based on firm, group and individual performance - Incentive compensation related to origination of new client sales - Top rated wellness program - Flexible working environment including remote and hybrid options &nbsp; &nbsp; Whatâs in it for you: - Working with an industry leader : Be part of a high-growth firm that is passionate for whatâs next. - An awesome culture:&nbsp; Thirty-one fundamental behaviors guide our culture every day ensuring we always deliver an exceptional team-member and client experience.&nbsp; We call it the Aprio Way.&nbsp; This shared mindset creates lasting relationships between team members and with clients. - A great team: &nbsp;Work with a high-energy, passionate, caring and ambitious team of professionals in a collaborative culture. - Entrepreneurship : Have the freedom to innovate and bring your ideas to help us grow to become the CPA firm of choice nationally. - Growth opportunities : Grow professionally in an environment that fosters continuous learning and advancement. - Competitive compensation : You will be rewarded with competitive compensation, industry-leading benefits and a flexible work environment to enjoy work/life balance. &nbsp; &nbsp; EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Aprio is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging diversity in the workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race; color; religion; national origin; sex; pregnancy; sexual orientation; gender identity and/or expression; age; disability; genetic information, citizenship status; military service obligations or any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. &nbsp; Aprio, LLP and Aprio Advisory Group, LLC, operate in an alternative business structure, with Aprio Advisory Group, LLC providing non-attest tax and consulting services, and Aprio, LLP providing CPA firm services. Please mention the word **ROMANTIC** and tag RMTM0LjEzOC40Mi4yMDk= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTM0LjEzOC40Mi4yMDk=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.

Are You Ready? &nbsp; CAI is a professional services company established in 1996 that has grown year over year to nearly 750 people worldwide. For Life Sciences and Mission Critical industries that need to deliver critical solutions in high-stakes environments, we provide accelerated operational readiness and unparalleled performance at the highest standard through our rigorous approach, field-tested processes, and elite expertise developed over 30 years. Our approach is simple because our purpose informs everything we do:â¯ &nbsp; We exist to be the trusted solution for our clients as they strive to build a better working world and improve human experience.â¯ &nbsp; At CAI, we are committed to living our Foundational Principles, both professionally and personally:â¯â¯ &nbsp; We act with integrity We serve each otherâ¯â¯ We serve societyâ¯â¯ We work for our future &nbsp; At CAI, we believe in a relentless dedication to excellence, pushing boundaries, and surpassing expectations. From the beginning, weâve challenged ourselves to do what others wouldnât. Not just setting industry standards but redefining them entirely. We are bold in our thinking and creative in our approach. We operate at the intersection of wisdom and technology and thrive when they come together with humanity. For us, operational readiness isnât simply a goal. Itâs a way of life. Because tomorrow demands to be at the forefront of today. We do this through tireless effort, precision, efficiency, and an unwavering belief that there is always room for advancement. Weâre not interested in how it used to be done. Weâre obsessed with how it will be done. &nbsp; We are seeking an experienced Recruiter to join our People Solutions Team and support our Life Sciences hiring in the Asia Pacific region. In this role, you will focus on sourcing, attracting, and hiring top talent for engineering roles within the life sciences and biotechnology spaces. The ideal candidate has experience recruiting in fast-paced, high-demand industries and understands the unique requirements of biotech environments. This role is a one year contract position.&nbsp; &nbsp; Key Responsibilities: Manage full-cycle recruitment across APAC (sourcing, screening, interviewing, offer negotiation, and onboarding support) with an emphasis in recruiting and hiring in Australia Partner with hiring managers in Life Sciences and Data Center teams to understand workforce needs and develop effective hiring strategies Source niche talent for roles such as: Biotech manufacturing (process engineers, validation engineers, QA/QC, MSAT, etc.) Data center commissioning (Cx engineers, MEP specialists, commissioning managers, etc.) Build and maintain strong pipelines of passive candidates using job boards, LinkedIn, referrals, and market mapping Develop regional market intelligence on talent availability, salary benchmarks, and competitor activity Ensure a high-quality candidate experience across all touchpoints Coordinate interviews across multiple time zones and stakeholders Maintain accurate data in the applicant tracking system (ATS) and generate recruiting reports Support employer branding and diversity hiring initiatives across APAC &nbsp; Qualifications: 3â7+ years of recruiting experience, preferably in technical or engineering hiring Proven experience recruiting in at least one of the following: Life Sciences / Biotech Manufacturing Data Center / Mission Critical Infrastructure Experience supporting hiring across Australia and APAC regions (e.g., Singapore, Australia, Japan, South Korea, India, etc.) Strong sourcing skills with experience identifying hard-to-find talent Ability to manage multiple requisitions in a fast-paced environment Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills Familiarity with the ATS system Lever and recruiting tools (e.g., LinkedIn Recruiter) Preferred Qualifications: Experience recruiting for commissioning or validation roles Understanding of GMP environments and/or mission-critical facility operations Experience working in a global or matrixed organization Ability to work flexible hours to support multiple time zones &nbsp; #LI-MV1&nbsp; 

 $55,000 - $75,000 a year Average base salary range. 
